  "review_conclusions": [
    "Action-time generation plus exact private worker-state identity is recorded under b.mu; start-time generation cannot authorize newer action evidence. Entry append and final detached clone recheck the same owner.",
    "Nonblocking enqueue, bounded receipt publication and rollback share b.mu. Pending receipt count is capped at queue256+workers4, including smaller test queues. Rejected sends leave no externally visible phantom obligation.",
    "Task defer retires each receipt exactly once on normal metadata completion, stale-owner return or panic; existing panic propagation is preserved. Retirement closes the private wake channel without claiming physical worker completion; existing physical joins remain untouched.",
    "One fixed accepted receipt set is waited with a5second child context shortened by parent cancellation/deadline. Context and lifecycle authority are rechecked under final snapshot lock; cancellation, timeout, worker loss or generation/identity replacement cannot produce an unqualified successful acquisition.",
    "Incomplete/unknown accepted work returns explicit bounded advisory WarningCodes and current evidence.incomplete, while preserving already captured partial entries. It does not set target error/success/duration or turn missing work into a zero traffic census.",
    "Current generation incomplete marker is bounded to one string per worker state; finishing stale receipts cannot poison a replacement generation or steal replacement pending obligations.",
    "Result applies the detached owned network snapshot without a second generic-buffer recapture. Deep cloning retains original absolute ring offsets and bounds.",
    "Ordinary nonoptin capture keeps its immediate legacy snapshot path without receipt wait/allocation. Existing queue/ring/body/metadata caps, callback native reads, target traffic, action timing, CPU sampling denominator and native80-resource>50acceptance remain unchanged.",
    "Existing protocol.BuildProtocolEvidence retains arbitrary bounded result.WarningCodes for inferred protocol and fallback evidence, supporting downstream advisory propagation."
